     1                                  ; E4 TS0 (agent2 day2 round 2, role E4, base DET2 rev2): zero-turn tandem split of captured b/d zombies.
     2                                  ; Mechanism (DET2 trace c360q; D1 emulator absim.mjs with b/d starts ~44/49 reproduces the traced A-kill rounds
     3                                  ;   4244/9414/10745/11146/12071): when BOTH zom20b and zom20d are captured within a few rounds (cohorts with a second
     4                                  ;   [0CC13h] writer: zchain/zrl03/ah02) they run B's template on the SAME anchor chain (phase 70h) a few rounds apart.
     5                                  ;   The leading trail triggers A's anchor, the trailing trail overwrites A's worker during the rebuild: A dies at
     6                                  ;   0.6k-15k rounds in 20 of 25 band combos (a lone b/d capture never kills A that early in the emulator).
     7                                  ; Change (B only, +6 bytes, same instruction count on both zombie paths): the CX=0 path swaps its BP (0, b/d zombies
     8                                  ;   never write BP) with the arena word [5D15h] (CCCCh until the first b/d capture; next to our [5D13h] hook) and
     9                                  ;   XORs 0BCCCh: the first b/d zombie gets 7000h (phase 70h exactly as DET2), every later one 0BCCCh (phase BCh,
    10                                  ;   19 lattice points away), so a tandem no longer shares one anchor chain. The dead 'mov bp,7000h' and the
    11                                  ;   b/d-useless 'xor di,di' before jcxz pay for the two new instructions; the zom20a path keeps xor di,di plus a nop.
    12                                  ;   Edit by agent2 day2 role E4; Good_Test V6 attribution below kept.
    13                                  ; D4 DET2: DET with B's [5D13h]/[0CC13h] writes back at instr 4/5 (rev1 rounds). DET's instr-3 [0CC13h]
    14                                  ; write tied with the zchain/zrl03/ah02 A write (instr 3) and lost the p0f13 hook half the time (screen n6sgd).
    15                                  ; D4 DET (day2, base rev1 KPHL): adaptive whole-team lattice. If a V6-family team is present (its B writes
    16                                  ; [4A17h] at instr 3; no other team in our fields writes that cell), every stream of ours (A, B, captured zombies)
    17                                  ; uses FAR_SEG 0FFAh = lattice 42h (10h below the V6-family 52h lattice, measured +0.28/+0.24 on leader2/3 cohorts
    18                                  ; in D4 W42 screen 0b3hc); otherwise FAR_SEG 0FFBh = 52h as in rev1 (W42's plain 2025/strong cost avoided).
    19                                  ; Detection: our B now writes [4A17h] late (instr 7), so at A's instr 5 and B's instr 5 the cell is still CCCCh
    20                                  ; unless a V6-family B wrote it at instr 3. A keeps the bit in BP; B patches the low byte of its own phoenix
    21                                  ; 'or dx,0FFBh' immediate (dec -> 0FAh) before any captured zombie can reach phoenix_init.
    22                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code (see the provenance comments below); DET edits by agent2 day2 role D4.
    23                                  ; COMBINE (night combination coordinator, 2026-10-04, base rev0): KPHL = KP + h34 (B099 KPH_B) + locpatA (B092 KL_A). A = KL_A unchanged; B = B099 KPH_B.
    24                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided code; V6nohunt and all night edits by agent2 roles (see FINDINGS.md).
    25                                  ; B099 (wave 10, domain 9 R5-cost): KPH = B094 KP + B089 h34 (CX=0 zombie path mov bp,3400h -> 7000h, 1 byte).
    26                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; K by A031 (E1+SD+Z1 by A031/A022/A026); p0f13 by B064/B084; KP by B094; h34 by B089.
    27                                  ; B094 (wave 9, domain 4 R5-cost): KP = A031 K (E1+SD+Z1) + B084 p0f13 B edits ported onto K_B (Z1+SD).
    28                                  ; Good_Test V6 is friend-provided; V6nohunt by agent2; Z1 by A026, SD by A022, E1/K by A031; p0f by B064, p0f13 by B084.
    29                                  ; p0f13 edits: startup push cs/pop es -> mov [0CC13h],bx + les di,[si+es_ptr] (INT87 stays instr 12); both b/d searches
    30                                  ;   (startup and zom20a path) use window 0F EB F9 CC -> 0F FF 26 13 (patched tail = jmp [0CC13h]).
    31                                  ; Port note: in the zom20a path DX is now 0CCF9h after INT87, so Z1's int 86h there would write FF 1F F9 CC junk
    32                                  ;   over E1's A block (0FF80h..007Fh). It is replaced by mov dx,0CCCCh (same instruction count, no INT86 there);
    33                                  ;   E1's A block already covers 0FF80h..007Fh. The b/d (CX=0) path INT86 block is unchanged.
    34                                  bits 16
    35                                  
    36                                  ; Good_Test V6 warrior 2 (friend-provided; reconstructed source in
    37                                  ; study-notes/good-test-v6/source/). agent2 label form: hard-coded internal
    38                                  ; offsets replaced by label arithmetic with the original operand widths.
    39                                  ; agent2 night A026 variant Z1 (base rev0 = V6nohunt B): captured zombies spend
    40                                  ; their own INT 86h charge (2 per zombie, unused before) on FF 1F CC CC decoy
    41                                  ; blocks for the FF1FCCCC INT87 searchers.
    42                                  ;  - zom20a path (CX!=0): after its b/d INT87, mov ax,1FFFh; int 86h with
    43                                  ;    DI=0, DF=1, DX=CCCCh -> block 0FF04h..0003h (no code is ever loaded below
    44                                  ;    400h or above FC00h; page FFh and 00h:00-03 hold no anchor of our 400h
    45                                  ;    lattice at 52h).
    46                                  ;  - b/d path (CX=0): the worthless 0E070E17 CC counter-bomb INT87 is replaced
    47                                  ;    by a block next to the zombie's own body (BX = own load address + 3):
    48                                  ;    [X+68h, X+168h), X = (BX and FC00h). Inside the zombie's MIN_GAP zone
    49                                  ;    and on pages 4k / 4k+1 outside in-page 52h-67h of pages 4k, so it can
    50                                  ;    hit neither loaded code nor any anchor/worker of our lattice.
    51                                  ;  - zombie band math uses 16-bit DIV (same AX, 2 instructions fewer), so both
    52                                  ;    zombie paths reach phoenix_init on the same turn as in rev0.
    53                                  ; B's own startup is unchanged.
    54                                  
    55                                  ; A031 K = A026 Z1 (zombie INT86 blocks) + A022 SD (phoenix_init mov cx,10; dead mov dx,[4A17h] dropped; db 0CCh,0CCh after the worker). B startup unchanged.
